        "label": "(c)(ii)",
        "question": "Explain the main factors that increase the risk of developing osteoporosis.",
        "marks": 12,
        "model": "3 factors @ 4 marks each \nGender: more common in females (especially post-menopausal women); diet: a lack of calcium and \nvitamin D in the diet; hereditary: family history can increase risk; age: risk increases with age; \nweight: considerable weight loss may also cause loss of bone mass; lack of weight bearing exercise \ncontributes to weakening of bones; disability: wheel chair and bed bound people are at risk due to \ninactivity; etc. \n\n(d)",
        "diagram": "",
