        "model": "• body measurements required \n2 points @ 2marks each \nNape to waist: measure from the most prominent bone at the base of the neck down to waistline; \nbust: bring the measuring tape around the fullest part of the bust and straight across the widest \npart of the back under the arms; waist: tie a string loosely around the waist to find the natural \nwaistline, measure over this with a measuring tape, do not pull the tape too tight; hips: usually 18 – \n23 cm below the waist, measure around the fullest part; trouser length: on the outside of the leg, \nmeasure from the waistline to the hem length, do the same on the inside of the leg; etc. \n\n• type of fabric you would select and reason for choice \nType of fabric: 2 marks, Reason: 2 marks \nCotton; polyester cotton; denim; viscose: etc. \n\n• outline plan of work to assemble the garment. \n4 points @ 2marks each \n(expect reference to underlined) \nPlan of work: layout/ pattern pieces on fabric; cutting; pin and tack pieces together; machine \nsewing/assembly/implementation; pressing/finishing; evaluation-fit and finish; etc. \n\nand \n2.(b)",
