        "question": "Using quorn mince, plan and set out the menu for a balanced three course meal suitable for a vegan.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "Balanced three-course vegan menu using vegan Quorn mince:\n\nStarter: homemade lentil and mixed-vegetable soup, served with a small wholemeal roll.\n\nMain course: vegan Quorn-mince chilli made with kidney beans, tomatoes, onions, peppers and sweetcorn; served with brown rice and a green side salad with lemon dressing.\n\nDessert: apple-and-berry oat crumble served with calcium-fortified soya custard.\n\nWater or unsweetened fruit juice may be offered as the beverage. This menu includes foods from the main food groups: vegetables and fruit; wholegrain carbohydrate; protein-rich pulses and Quorn; and a fortified dairy alternative. The courses also vary in colour, flavour, texture and cooking method. All stock, margarine, custard and Quorn used must be checked to ensure that they are specifically labelled vegan and contain no meat, dairy or egg ingredients.",
