        "label": "",
        "question": "Outline the role of the Food Safety Authority of Ireland (FSAI). Give three points.",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "The Food Safety Authority of Ireland protects public health by coordinating and enforcing food-safety and hygiene legislation throughout the food chain. It monitors food businesses and works with official agencies on inspections, sampling, traceability, alerts, product withdrawals and recalls. It also gives consumers and food businesses authoritative advice, publishes safety information and investigates food-safety concerns so that food sold in Ireland is safe and honestly presented.",
        "diagram": "",
        "source_page": 5,
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
