        "question": "Describe the following types of pensions.\nContributory old age pension\nNon-Contributory old age pension",
        "marks": 6,
        "model": "The contributory old-age pension is a State pension based on the claimant’s record of Pay Related Social Insurance contributions. It is not means-tested, so other income does not normally remove entitlement. The non-contributory old-age pension is a means-tested social-assistance payment for an older person who lacks enough qualifying PRSI contributions. Eligibility and the rate paid depend on the person’s means and habitual residence.",
        "diagram": "",
        "source_page": 6,
        "model_source": "ai-h1"
