        "marks": 18,
        "model": "Breakfast: a small glass of unsweetened orange juice; porridge made with low-fat milk and topped with berries; one slice of wholemeal toast; water or tea. This supplies wholegrain carbohydrate and fibre for slow energy, vitamin C and one dairy serving. Lunch: homemade vegetable and lentil soup with a wholemeal roll; natural yoghurt and an apple; water. Lentils provide protein and iron, while vegetables and fruit help reach the recommended five to seven daily portions. Main meal: baked chicken breast with a broccoli-and-cheddar cheese sauce, boiled baby potatoes and carrots; fresh fruit salad; water or milk. The chicken supplies lean HBV protein and iron; potatoes supply carbohydrate; vegetables add fibre and vitamins; and a measured portion of cheddar contributes calcium, protein and flavour. The menu follows the food pyramid by basing meals on vegetables, fruit and wholegrain starchy foods, including three dairy servings, choosing lean protein, using low-fat cooking methods and keeping foods high in fat, sugar and salt to a minimum. Portions should match age, sex and activity, and water should be taken regularly.",
