        "model": "Extra Light Spread has the lowest energy, total fat and saturated fat, so is most suitable for weight reduction and reducing CHD risk; it has three times the PUFA of butter but less than Original. Original Spread is intermediate in energy, total fat and saturates; it has about four times Extra Light's monounsaturates and the highest PUFA level, which may lower total and LDL cholesterol. Butter has the highest energy, total fat and saturated fat, so is least suitable for weight reduction and may raise total and LDL cholesterol; it has the most monounsaturates but the least PUFA. Omega-3 lowers cholesterol and CHD risk; trans fats may raise LDL and lower HDL; excessive sodium may cause hypertension and increase CHD/stroke risk.",
