        "label": "(b)",
        "question": "Describe the stages in a basic Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Point (HACCP) system for making a hot meat dish. Refer to (i) possible hazards and (ii) the corresponding control measures to be implemented.",
        "marks": 24,
        "model": "Purchase—hazards: damaged goods, bacterial/chemical contamination and pests; controls: use a reputable shop, separate raw and cooked foods, inspect packaging/dates/temperatures and pest damage, and transport perishables in refrigerator bags. Storage—hazards: bacterial multiplication and cross-contamination; controls: chill below 5°C, freeze below −18°C and check vegetables for mould. Preparation—hazards: multiplication and cross-contamination; controls: wash hands with antibacterial soap, use colour-coded boards and wash equipment in hot water and detergent. Cooking—hazard: surviving bacteria; control: core temperature 74°C for two minutes. Serving/hot holding—hazards: cross-contamination and growth of survivors; controls: clean utensils, hold above 63°C for no more than 1½ hours, reheat once only and cover/store correctly before reheating.",
