        "question": "Differentiate between regenerated fibres and synthetic fibres and give one example of each.",
        "marks": 9,
        "model": "Regenerated fibres are made from cellulose that is pulped, chemically treated and forced through nozzles, e.g. rayon, viscose or acetate. Synthetic fibres are made from chemicals such as coal or petroleum, e.g. nylon, polyester, acrylic or PVC.",
