        "marks": 9,
        "model": "To lengthen a commercial trouser pattern, use the printed lengthen-or-shorten line, which is at right angles to the grainline.\n\n    original piece       lengthened piece\n       ↑ grain              ↑ grain\n    ┌────────┐           ┌────────┐\n    │        │           │        │\n    ├─cut────┤           ├────────┤\n    │        │           │ paper  │ ← required extra length\n    └────────┘           ├────────┤\n                         │        │\n                         └────────┘\n\nCut along the line. Place extra paper underneath and spread the two pattern sections evenly by the required amount, keeping the grainline sections aligned and parallel. Tape securely, extend the grainline, and use a ruler or French curve to redraw smooth side seams. Transfer all notches and construction marks before cutting the fabric. The same amount must be added to matching front and back pieces.",
